EXT. DRAINED POOL SKATE BOWL - DUSK

Cracked turquoise concrete. Graffiti tags. A chain-link fence with a hole cut in it. Orange sky.

SADIE PRZYBYLSKI, sixteen, crouches at the lip with her board, knuckles whitened. At the bottom of the bowl, JUNO TEAGUE-BALOGUN, seventeen, spins a wheel with one finger. Ten feet away, her friend OLU, seventeen, sits on the edge, a camera in his lap, not filming.

Nobody has said a word in a while.

JUNO
You're going to fall.

SADIE
I know.

JUNO
So why?

Sadie shrugs. She drops in. Wheels roar on concrete. She carves up the far wall, hangs for one stalled instant, and the board skids sideways from under her.

She hits the bowl floor hard. Juno is on her feet. Olu is on his feet. All three hover.

OLU
You good?

SADIE
(laughing, wincing)
Yeah.

She sits up. A bloodied elbow. Juno kneels. Olu raises the camera, then lowers it again.

JUNO
Let me see.

SADIE
It's nothing.

JUNO
It's something.

Sadie pulls her arm away. Juno lets her. They sit. Olu sits too. The sky goes violet over the bowl, and a streetlight buzzes on.

OLU
My dad's picking me up at eight.

SADIE
Okay.

JUNO
Okay.

Nobody moves.
